action  :: 'Monitor_Anhedonia' ;
     caption :: 'Monitor mood, anhedonia, and suicidality' ;
     description :: 'Monitors reduced enjoyment of life / anhedonia and possible mood change as a mechanism-of-action harm of GLP-1 reward-pathway modulation (Prescribe_GLP1). GLP-1 acts on central reward pathways, and the ADA 2026 Standards list mood changes among the items to monitor on semaglutide (Table 2.1); the current Wegovy label (revised 02/2026) no longer carries a Suicidal Behavior and Ideation warning, so the suicidality screen is an assistant-selected safeguard; PHQ-9 and C-SSRS are validated mood/suicidality screens.' ;
     metaprops :: 'applies_when=all_patients_on_therapy
assistant_invention=operationalization as PHQ-9 plus C-SSRS at the GLP-1 follow-up cadence; SNOMED coded as the anhedonia finding (narrower than the combined mood and suicidality screen)
category=undesired_ade
cq=CQ7
goal.noun_phrase=mood and anhedonia screen (PHQ-9) with suicidality screen (C-SSRS), baseline then each visit (monthly x3, then q3mo)
goal.verb=order
guideline_status=not_specified_as_a_guideline_monitoring_task
instrument=PHQ-9 and C-SSRS questionnaires
knowledge_origin=skill prompted the mechanism (reward-pathway modulation reducing enjoyment) then assistant selected validated instruments independently
literature_basis=GLP-1 acts on central reward pathways, and the ADA 2026 Standards list mood changes among the items to monitor on semaglutide (Table 2.1); the current Wegovy label (revised 02/2026) no longer carries a Suicidal Behavior and Ideation warning, so the suicidality screen is an assistant-selected safeguard; PHQ-9 and C-SSRS are validated mood/suicidality screens
monitored_target=reduced enjoyment of life / anhedonia and possible mood change as a mechanism-of-action harm of GLP-1 reward-pathway modulation (Prescribe_GLP1)
monitoring_frequency_basis=mirrors GLP-1 follow-up visits so mood is screened whenever the drug is reviewed
monitoring_stance=recommended
ontology.coding=SNOMED\\:28669007
ontology.label=Anhedonia (finding)
order.code=mood and anhedonia screen (PHQ-9) with suicidality screen (C-SSRS)
order.patient_instruction=report loss of interest or pleasure, low mood, reduced motivation, or thoughts of self-harm
order.performer_instruction=if PHQ-9 elevated or any suicidality, administer C-SSRS and refer per protocol
order.timing=baseline then each visit (monthly x3, then q3mo)
provenance_type=mechanism_prompted_then_assistant_independent_literature_search_and_operationalized
quote.1=p.4, Table 2.1 (Semaglutide, Clinical suggestions and monitoring)\\: "Monitor \\u2022 Heart rate \\u2022 Mood changes"
source.1=ADA 2026 Standards of Care in Overweight and Obesity, Pharmacologic Treatment of Obesity in Adults, Table 2.1 (p.4) semaglutide clinical suggestions and monitoring
source.2=PHQ-9 Patient Health Questionnaire-9 (Kroenke K, J Gen Intern Med 2001;16\\:606)
source.3=Columbia-Suicide Severity Rating Scale (C-SSRS, Posner K, Am J Psychiatry 2011;168\\:1266)
source_kind=clinical_guideline_plus_screening_instrument
trigger=positive depression screen or any suicidal ideation prompts same-day C-SSRS and referral
' ;
     procedure :: 'Mood and anhedonia screen (PHQ-9) with suicidality screen (C-SSRS), baseline then each visit (monthly x3, then q3mo). Patient: report loss of interest or pleasure, low mood, reduced motivation, or thoughts of self-harm. Clinician: if PHQ-9 elevated or any suicidality, administer C-SSRS and refer per protocol.' ;
end action.

